<title>INDIA: India M3 money supply falls to 15.6 pct on Mar 28.</title>
<headline>India M3 money supply falls to 15.6 pct on Mar 28.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's year-on-year M3 money supply growth was 15.6 percent on March 28, 1997, down from 15.8 percent on March 14, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.  </p>
<p>		   M3 MONEY SUPPLY GROWTH (yr-on-yr in pct)</p>
<p>		   Mar 28, 1997   Mar 14, 1997  Mar 29, 1996</p>
<p>		   15.6	     15.8	    13.41</p>
<p>Money supply was 6,990.52 billion rupees on March 28, 1997 against 6,830.24 billion on March 14, the RBI said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
